{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","$id":"https://rendel.ai/schemas/setup/v1.json","title":"Rendel setup file (version 1)","description":"The Rendel setup file, rendel/setup.json. A coding agent describes the app in it; the developer imports it into their Rendel console (rendel.ai). Writing it sends nothing anywhere.\n\n1. Add the Rendel SDK. Flutter: the `rendel` package as a git dependency from https://github.com/neon-apps/rendel-flutter (its newest tag), with Rendel.init in main() before runApp. Website: the script tag from https://rendel.ai/sdk/web/ on every page. Both take the app's TEST publishable key (rd_pk_test_…): ask the developer for it (Rendel console → Settings → Keys & environments), or leave a clearly named placeholder and list the swap in human_todos. Publishable keys are the only keys that go into code.\n2. If the app has sign-in: call Rendel.identify with the app's own user id where sign-in succeeds and where a saved session is restored, Rendel.reset() on sign-out, and give the SDK the signed-in user's token (`userToken` in RendelConfig on Flutter, Rendel.setUserToken on the web), so Rendel calls the app's API as that user. Passing it to the SDK is intended; a token's value never goes in this file.\n3. Describe the app here. Each property says what it is and how to fill it. Only version, app and summary are required: leave out a section you have nothing for. Make code edits with your file-edit tool.\n4. Add rendel/setup.json to .gitignore. Never put secrets, .env contents, API keys or end users' data in it: the import refuses a file holding anything that looks like a credential.\n5. Last, tell the developer to import it: the Rendel console shows the command, `curl -fsS -H \"Authorization: Bearer <import code>\" -F manifest=@rendel/setup.json -F logo=@<logoPath> \"https://rendel.ai/api/setup/import\"`, or they drop the file on the console's Overview.\n\nA sync (the app is set up already) is the same file, written again as the code is now. Items are matched by external_key (screens by name): an unchanged item stays as it is, and one removed from the code goes in as an archive entry. On a live app every change waits for the developer's review.\n\nThe file is at most 2 MB. A file holding only version, app and knowledge is accepted too: when the knowledge would push a file past 2 MB, put some of it in such a file and import that first.","anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"$schema":{"description":"\"https://rendel.ai/schemas/setup/v1.json\", so editors validate the file.","type":"string","maxLength":300},"version":{"type":"number","const":1,"description":"Always 1."},"app":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-z0-9](?:[a-z0-9-]{0,38}[a-z0-9])?$","description":"The app's slug, as the developer's prompt names it (\"for my app grove\" → \"grove\"). The import refuses a file for another app."},"detected":{"type":"object","properties":{"platform":{"description":"flutter | web | nextjs | react | …","type":"string","maxLength":40},"framework":{"type":"string","maxLength":80},"router":{"type":"string","maxLength":80},"http":{"type":"string","maxLength":80},"auth":{"type":"string","maxLength":200},"locales":{"maxItems":40,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","maxLength":16}},"screens":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":10000},"apiCalls":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":10000},"themeFile":{"type":"string","maxLength":300},"darkTheme":{"description":"Whether the app has a dark theme of its own.","type":"boolean"},"fonts":{"maxItems":10,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","maxLength":80}},"logoFile":{"type":"string","maxLength":300},"signIn":{"description":"The app's own sign-in on its API that takes an account and a password (or nothing secret). Left out for Firebase, Supabase, OAuth or a one-time code.","type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string","maxLength":2000,"pattern":"^https:\\/\\/\\S+$","description":"The full https address, e.g. `https://api.example.com/v1/auth/login`."},"fields":{"minItems":1,"maxItems":12,"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,63}$"},"secret":{"description":"A password or PIN.","type":"boolean"},"required":{"description":"Defaults to true.","type":"boolean"},"type":{"type":"string","enum":["string","integer","number","boolean"]},"format":{"description":"`email`, `date`, `password`…","type":"string","maxLength":40}},"required":["name"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"The JSON body's fields, by name. Never a value."}},"required":["url","fields"],"additionalProperties":false},"signUp":{"description":"The app's own sign-up on its API: the request that creates a user. Left out when there is none.","type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string","maxLength":2000,"pattern":"^https:\\/\\/\\S+$","description":"The full https address, e.g. `https://api.example.com/v1/auth/login`."},"fields":{"minItems":1,"maxItems":12,"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,63}$"},"secret":{"description":"A password or PIN.","type":"boolean"},"required":{"description":"Defaults to true.","type":"boolean"},"type":{"type":"string","enum":["string","integer","number","boolean"]},"format":{"description":"`email`, `date`, `password`…","type":"string","maxLength":40}},"required":["name"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"The JSON body's fields, by name. Never a value."}},"required":["url","fields"],"additionalProperties":false},"repo":{"description":"Where this app's code is, so connecting GitHub in the console can choose it in one click.","type":"object","properties":{"remote":{"description":"What `git remote get-url origin` prints.","type":"string","maxLength":300},"branch":{"description":"The default branch, e.g. main.","type":"string","maxLength":255},"roots":{"maxItems":4,"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"platform":{"type":"string","enum